    <string name="lemuroid_help_content"><![CDATA[
        <b>&#8226;How do I use Retro Game System?</b><br/>
        Copy all your ROMs files into a directory on your device and select it within Retro Game System. This directory is allowed to have subdirectories. After the scan completes you should see your games.<br/><br/>
        <b>&#8226;Why aren\'t my games detected?</b><br/>
        If your games are compressed, try uncompressing them. If this doesn\'t work try putting ROMs into separate directories, one for each system with the following names: $SYSTEMS.
    ]]></string>

    <string name="lemuroid_crash_disclamer">It looks like the Libretro core has experienced an unexpected issue. If it\'s persistent please try the following:\n
        \n\u2022 Disable auto-save and re-run the game
        \n\u2022 Go into Android settings and clear the app cache
        \n\u2022 Go into Retro Game System settings and perform a Factory Reset
        \n\n If none of the above works, it might be possible that this Game/Core is not supported by this device.
    </string>

    <string name="lemuroid_app_error_disclamer">The app hit an internal error and had to close the game. This is not a problem with your game, your ROM or the emulation core, so clearing data or resetting won\'t help. Sending us the message below is what gets it fixed.</string>

    <!-- The core stopped answering the render thread. Neither of the two disclaimers above fits:
         it is not an app bug, and clearing data or a factory reset cannot reach a stuck thread. -->
    <string name="lemuroid_core_stalled_disclamer">The emulation core stopped responding and the game had to be closed. This is not a problem with your device or your ROM, so clearing data or resetting won\'t help. Open the game again — any progress since your last save may have been lost.</string>

